        <body>
            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="0791" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg683"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1893</hi></date>. (Received October 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 68.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In answer to a telegram to Mosul, I was
                    informed by telegram by Dr. McDowell that the case against parties arrested for
                    assault on Miss Melton was suffering from needless delay. The governor of the
                    province, who the grand vizier says he regards as culpable, has been removed by
                    him, and his successor, who lives here, has started to relieve him. He will
                    require twenty days to make the journey, and the grand vizier assures me that on
                    his arrival at Mosul speedy punishment will be inflicted upon the guilty
                    parties.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
